  "query_preview": "/Friday through Tuesday/...\nIssued 318 AM MDT TUE JUL 28 2026\nWith troughing over British Columbia and high pressure aloft \nover the Four Corners region, hot, dry, and breezy conditions \nwill continue through the end of the week. As such, the dense \nwildfire smoke coverage will likely not see improvements towards\nthe weekend. The long-term forecast has temperatures climbing \naround 5 degrees above normal Friday and Saturday, but dense \nsmoke may continue to slightly moderate the peak temperatures \ndue to limited daytime mixing. Come Sunday, the aforementioned \nBritish Columbia trough will steer into our area and bring a dry\ncold frontal passage. Gusty winds and near or even slightly \nbelow normal temperatures will be expected Sunday through \nMonday. Tuesday will see a slight warming to near normal \ntemperatures. Otherwise, considerably dry conditions will \npersist through the extended period.",
